course: dictionary
lesson: 12878
title: Words that follow on
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Ensuing is a formal word. It means coming after something, usually as its result. «The power cut plunged the street into darkness, and in the ensuing chaos, nobody could find a torch.» The chaos came straight after the power cut, because of it, so ensuing means coming after.
explain: Look for clues. «The bell rang. In the ensuing silence, the teacher began to speak.» Before the word, the bell rang. After the word, the teacher speaks. The silence came next, so ensuing means following.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping in simpler words. «The following silence» or «the silence that came after» both make sense, so you have it right.
fact: Ensuing is an adjective, and it comes from the verb ensue.
fact: «Ensuing» means coming after something, usually as its result.
fact: «Ensuing» can also mean next in time, as in «the ensuing days».
fact: You will often meet ensuing in news reports, formal writing and exam texts.
fact: In everyday speech, people say «the following» or «what came after».
exercise: «The storm knocked out the power. In the ensuing darkness, the children lit candles.» What does ensuing mean here? | Quiet and still | Very dark and scary | *Coming after the storm, as its result | Happy and loud
exercise: «The two teams argued, and the ensuing fight stopped the match.» Which words mean about the same as ensuing here? | *the fight that followed | the funny fight | the last fight ever | the fight in the rain
exercise: Which word fits best in «The rain stopped, and the ___ weeks were sunny.»? | quiet | purple | *ensuing | sleepy
test: «The loud crash was followed by the ensuing panic in the shop.» What does ensuing mean? | Quiet and calm | Happening before the crash | Very expensive | *Happening after the crash, as a result
test: In «the ensuing weeks», what does ensuing tell us about the weeks? | *They came after the event | They were the best weeks ever | They lasted only one day | They came before the event
exam: «After the earthquake, the ensuing flood ruined many homes.» Which best explains ensuing? | The flood was small and harmless | The earthquake was caused by the flood | *The flood came after the earthquake, as a result of it | The flood came before the earthquake
